rties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A simple culture medium which is obtained by providing a suspension in an alcohol containing (a) 0.01 to 0.4 wt % of an adhesive being soluble in water and an alcohol, (b) a gelling agent being soluble in water and insoluble in an alcohol and (c) nutritive components for bacteria, impregnating a fibrous, water-absorbent sheet having a mesh larger than that of the gelling agent which is placed on a waterproof flat plate with the alcohol suspension, and drying the resultant plate with the sheet while suppressing the rapid evaporation of the alcohol, to thereby bond the water-absorbent sheet to the waterproof flat plate; and a method for preparing the simple culture medium.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne un milieu de culture simple que l'on obtient en apportant une suspension dans un alcool contenant a) de 0,01 à 0,4 % en poids d'un adhésif hydrosoluble et un alcool, b) un agent gélifiant hydrosoluble et insoluble dans un alcool et c) des composants alimentaires pour des bactéries, en imprégnant une feuille fibreuse, absorbant l'eau et présentant un treillis plus large que celui de l'agent gélifiant qui se trouve sur une plaque imperméable avec la suspension d'alcool. Puis on sèche la plaque obtenue avec la feuille tout en supprimant l'évaporation rapide de l'alcool pour lier la feuille absorbant l'eau à la plaque imperméable. L'invention concerne aussi un procédé de préparation du milieu de culture simple.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>